==============================================================================
d(x) for x = 1 .. 64: 2221221222122122212212221221222122212212221221222122122212212221
one spatial period of 32 Nodes: 23 Nodes of dwell 2, 9 of dwell 1, the sum 55 = 55 intervals of the flight period
the identity claimed: 55 arrivals at a Node become 55 x 55 / 32 = 3025/32 row-intervals of presence;
   at ONE Node over 55 intervals the presence is 55 x d(x) = 55 or 110 row-intervals, never 94.53125
   over the 32 Nodes of a spatial period (one interval): presence 55 rows; x c = 32 / 55 -> 32 = the 32 arrivals: exact, remainder 0
   at one Node: presence x c per interval = d(x) x 32 / 55 = 32/55 or 64/55 of the beam's rate: -41.8 % or +16.4 %, a factor, not a remainder

